@page "/"

<PageTitle>BCJS — Chart.js for Blazor</PageTitle>

<h1>BCJS sample</h1>

<p>
    A clean <strong>net10.0</strong> reimplementation of a Blazor Chart.js wrapper, running
    <strong>Chart.js 4.5.1</strong> via an isolated ES module (no global script tags). Each demo below
    renders a chart and exercises the interactive API — <em>add data</em>, <em>update</em>, and
    <em>destroy</em> (by toggling the component in and out of the render tree).
</p>

<ul>
    <li><a href="line">Line</a> — multi-dataset line chart, add-data and update.</li>
    <li><a href="bar">Bar</a> — vertical bars, add a dataset at runtime.</li>
    <li><a href="pie-doughnut">Pie &amp; Doughnut</a> — two configs side by side.</li>
    <li><a href="radar">Radar</a> — radial scale with a filled dataset.</li>
    <li><a href="mixed">Mixed</a> — bar + line on one chart via per-dataset type.</li>
    <li><a href="dashboard-pie">Dashboard pie</a> — styled tooltip, round legend markers, percentage labels.</li>
    <li><a href="html-legend">HTML legend</a> — a sharp, clickable legend beside the chart; browser-side number formats.</li>
    <li><a href="time-axis">Time axis</a> — dates spaced by time with the bundled date-fns adapter; wheel, drag and pinch zoom.</li>
    <li><a href="data-update">Data updates</a> — switch a range filter; charts redraw in place.</li>
    <li><a href="custom-tooltip">Custom tooltip</a> — tooltip content from your own JavaScript function.</li>
</ul>
